{
  "name": "Start",
  "comment": "Fix, then go on from the same step: Work reads a file that isn't there yet, and its handler fixes the cause (writes\nthe file), then starts the error's callback. The callback goes on from the read, in an app of its own: the read runs\nagain, finds the file, and the run goes on to its end, answering what it read. The handler checks that answer; the\nresumed run never reaches the handler, as its read no longer fails.",
  "step": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "call Work",
      "line": {
        "number": 6,
        "indent": 0
      },
      "code": [
